../../../../study/video-digests/2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3/digest.md:35:### T03 — The 2% bar chart (a number drawn as a height insult)
../../../../study/video-digests/2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3/digest.md-36-- **Timestamps:** ≈6–18 s.
../../../../study/video-digests/2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3/digest.md-37-- **Mechanics:** four tall empty bar outlines rise to a 100% axis; a tiny filled stub labelled ۲٪ (2%) appears at the base of the first bar while the star figure stands at the right at full height. The spoken contrast — "a thing has a 2% chance; I wait for the 2%; you wait for the 100%" (gloss) — lands on the visual disproportion.
../../../../study/video-digests/2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3/digest.md-38-- **Why it works:** the argument's central quantity is felt as a height ratio before it is understood as a statistic; the empty bars are the humans' expectation, drawn hollow.
../../../../study/video-digests/2026-11-18-ig-dffiipmmac3/digest.md-39-- **Evidence:** ev/010-two-percent-bars.jpg. Form: frame.
